    "updated_at": "2026-11-13T01:04:36Z",
    "body": "This conflicts with main in one place, and it is the same logic changed on both sides, so it was not auto-resolved.\n\nFile: crates/app/src/operation/job.rs, function collect_job, the first material read.\n- This PR: replaces the read with `let opframe = OpFrame::of(op); let material = opframe.material_of(world, &op.src)?;`, routing it through the new frame seam (frame.rs `OpFrame::material_of` -> `material::material_of`).\n- main (PR #1064, reduced-fidelity laws): changed the same line to `super::material::judged_material(world, setup, &op.src)?`. `judged_material` calls `material_of` and then raises `m.excess` to the worst of the part's and the stock entity's (`model_fidelity::excess_of`) for non-Stock sources, so the collision laws see a coarse stock model.\n\nA plain merge would either drop main's excess adjustment (a weakened safety check) or bypass the seam. Suggested resolution for the author: give `OpFrame` a judged variant (or have `OpFrame::material_of` call `judged_material`) so collect_job keeps `opframe` and also gets main's excess rule, then check no other `material_of` caller of the seam needs the same. Please merge origin/main on this branch, resolve that hunk by hand, re-run the targeted gate and push.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
